  "note": "Election of the Aughnacloy Town Commissioners, polled Monday 15 January 1923. Nine Unionists were returned unopposed; the Sinn Feiners, with a small majority of 18 against them, nominated no candidates (Armagh Guardian, 12 January 1923, p. 3). All nine were Unionists; no contest. Returned unopposed."
